  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;be the focus of the parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;and the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;intersect the parabola at two points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>. Let the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be the centroid of the triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math>. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;"
  },
